 "why_this_round": {
  "the_answer_being_tested": "a program can only refuse on a condition it checks, and its refusal says which -- so one controlled violation per property enumerates a sufficient vocabulary, with no trace-completeness assumption and nothing inferred from successes",
  "the_gap_it_closes": "every prior round and every action-model-learning paper takes the fact vocabulary as an input; the insufficiency certificate says that is where the wall is",
  "why_it_could_fail": "if the surface is unbounded; if message classes merge properties that vary independently, making the grain unsound; if single-property refusals do not predict joint unexecuted states; if one experience is already enough"
 }
